Indonesian district point supplement
===================================

Contains information from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/), licensed
under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
Full license: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt and
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode .

Source: https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/allCountries.zip
Cached snapshot: 2026-10-27. The content hash, counts, transformations and
crosswalk abstentions are recorded in id-admin-points.sources.json.
GeoNames provides the data as is, without warranty of accuracy, timeliness
or completeness. GeoNames administrative points do not establish surveyed
seats, populated settlements, current boundaries or district containment.

Modification: prepare-id-admin-points.py selects Indonesian ADM3 records
with unique, bidirectional name/province matches to the pinned Indonesian
names-and-codes hierarchy. Supplied GeoNames county codes must agree through
their own name crosswalk. GeoNames, Kemendagri and BPS codes are not treated
as interchangeable. ADM4 is audited but is not imported as settlement data.
The builder additionally requires unique containing county geometry, rejects
ambiguous existing district mappings and preserves established coordinates.
No coordinates are inferred from settlements or generated from centroids.

Names/code crosswalk: cahyadsn/wilayah, copyright Cahya DSN, MIT.
The full upstream MIT notice, pinned revision and provenance are retained in
id-hierarchy.NOTICE and id-hierarchy.sources.json alongside this supplement.
Both sources retain their own licenses. No endorsement is implied.
